---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GraphExplorer from '../../components/GraphExplorer.jsx';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../../data/seo';

const meta = seo.studio;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-standards.pages.dev/';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: meta.title,
  description: meta.description,
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, meta.canonicalPath),
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath}
  ogType={meta.ogType}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="studio-wrapper container">
    <div class="tensor-panel studio-intro-card">
      <h2>Published graph and layer editor</h2>
      <p>Graph Studio imports, combines, and exports public graphs with vendor and organization layers. The layer pack preserves product and policy annotations separately from the base question fields. Added questions and routes provide their own definitions.</p>
      <p><a href="/extensions/">Layering guide and formats</a> · <a href="/studio/?graph=0.20260206e&amp;example=cloud-layers&amp;node=Q4">Cloud layering example</a> · <a href="/examples/layers/cloud-investigation.layers.json" download>Example layer pack</a></p>
      <p>This editor uses the published graph format. Its local checks cover node and route structure. The <a href="/graphs/">Atlas</a> provides the working public graph, 3D views, and guided investigations; the <a href="/investigation-lab/">Lab</a> provides Core record validation and exchange.</p>
    </div>

    <GraphExplorer client:load />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
